e is expressed on early murine hematopoietic progenitors and regulates their numbers in sites of hematopoiesis. <source>Immunity.</source> <volume>19</volume>:<fpage>33</fpage>&#x02013;45.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12871637</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib41"><label>41</label><citation citation-type="journal">Bosse, R., and D. Vestweber. <year>1994</year>. Only simultaneous blocking of the L- and P-selectin completely inhibits neutrophil migration into mouse peritoneum. <source>Eur. J. Immunol.</source> <volume>24</volume>:<fpage>3019</fpage>&#x02013;3024.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7528665</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib42"><label>42</label><citation citation-type="journal">Dimmeler, S., A. Aicher, M. Vasa, C. Mildner-Rihm, K. Adler, M. Tiemann, H. Rutten, S. Fichtlscherer, H. Martin, and A.M. Zeiher. <year>2001</year>. HMG-CoA reductase inhibitors (statins) increase endothelial progenitor cells via the PI 3-kinase/Akt pathway. <source>J. Clin. Invest.</source> <volume>108</volume>:<fpage>391</fpage>&#x02013;397.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11489932</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>